      "content": "While clotrimazole can help treat fungal infections like ringworm, it's essential to get it checked by a doctor first to confirm the exact cause. Clotrimazole may not be effective against bacterial or viral causes, and overusing it without proper diagnosis can lead to antibiotic resistance. In the meantime, keeping the affected area clean and dry, and wearing loose, breathable clothing can help. Apply a cool compress and avoid scratching the area to prevent further irritation.",
